      "type": "teach",
      "title": "𐑩 vs 𐑳",
      "body": "Both are “uh” sounds, and stress is what separates them. 𐑳 (up) is the one a stressed syllable gets — cup, sun, bus. 𐑩 (ado) is its unstressed shadow: say again, then until, and notice how little of the first syllable you actually pronounce."
